Basis of preparation and important notice
 
Purpose
This report compares four listed participants in India's renewable energy build-out on five dimensions: revenue growth, debt structure, EBITDA, valuation multiples and ESG. It is a screening and diligence document. It sets out what the reported numbers show, where they have been estimated, and how confident a reader should be in each figure.

Sources
Financial data is taken from audited FY2025-26 consolidated results, exchange filings under Regulation 33, results press releases, investor presentations and earnings calls. Market data is taken from NSE and BSE closing prices. ESG data is taken from MSCI, Morningstar Sustainalytics, LSEG, S&P Global's Corporate Sustainability Assessment, CRISIL ESG Ratings & Analytics and Corporate Knights. A full source register is at Appendix E.

Estimated figures
Three of the four companies do not publish a clean gross-debt-and-equity split in their results releases; they publish leverage ratios instead. Total equity has therefore been reverse-engineered from the reported ratio and the reported debt. Every such figure is flagged, and each estimate has been tested by computing price-to-book from it and comparing against independently published market ratios. The reconciliation is set out at section 9.3. Readers should treat flagged figures as indicative and replace them once all FY2025-26 annual reports are filed.

Comparability
The four companies are deliberately not comparables. They occupy different positions on the same value chain: an integrated utility, two independent power producers and an equipment manufacturer. Certain multiples — EV/Revenue in particular — carry no cross-sectional meaning in this set, and the report says so where that applies rather than presenting the number without comment.

No forward estimates
Everything in this report is historical and reported. There are no consensus forecasts, no discounted cash flow, no target prices and no recommendations. Section 9.4 describes how the underlying model extends to forward multiples without structural change.

Disclaimer
This document has been prepared for information purposes only. It does not constitute investment research, an offer or a solicitation, and it is not advice on the merits of any security. Figures are derived from sources believed to be reliable but no representation is made as to their accuracy or completeness. Past performance is not indicative of future results.

