Three observations.
Margin tells you the business model; return on equity tells you the investment. Adani Green and NTPC Green post the highest EBITDA margins in the set and the lowest returns on equity. There is no contradiction: a contracted IPP earns a high margin on a very large asset base, and the return depends entirely on how much of that base is earning. Suzlon posts the lowest EBITDA margin and by far the highest return on equity, because it turns its capital over.
NTPC Green's 2.8% return on equity is the weakest number in this report. It sits below the company's own cost of debt. That is defensible for a business two years into a build cycle, provided the commissioning schedule delivers. It is not defensible indefinitely, and it is the single metric most worth tracking quarter to quarter.
Suzlon's 33.4% return on equity should be discounted before it is relied upon. Strip the ₹742 crore deferred tax credit and return on equity falls to roughly 25.6% — still the highest in the set by a wide margin, but a different number from the headline.

