7.4  The correlation is real, and close to circular
Across the three rated names, the ESG composite and the EV/EBITDA multiple move together. It would be easy, and wrong, to present that as evidence of a green premium.
The highest-scoring company is also the purest-play renewable one, and purity of exposure is what the multiple is already pricing — as section 6.2 sets out independently of any ESG consideration. With three observations there is no statistical claim available. The relationship shown in Exhibit 11 is best understood as two views of the same underlying variable rather than as one causing the other.
What the analysis does establish is narrower and more useful: an ESG-screened mandate would rank these four very differently from a growth-screened one, and one of them would not pass the screen at all for want of a rating.

