9.4  Updating the model
The model was built so that refreshing it is a data task, not an analytical one.
– New results. Add one row per company to Fact_Financials and Fact_Operations, add the year to Dim_FiscalYear and move the Is Latest FY marker. Every ratio, growth rate, CAGR, multiple and exhibit recalculates.
– Price movement. Edit only the Close Price and Price Date fields in Fact_Market. Market capitalisation, enterprise value, EV/EBITDA, price-to-earnings and price-to-book all follow.
– New ESG rating. Enter the score in the relevant agency column. The normalisation formula, the agency count and the composite recalculate, and the company joins Exhibit 11 automatically. This is specifically how NTPC Green's missing rating is absorbed when it publishes.
– Changing thresholds. The leverage bands (3.0x and 6.0x) and the ESG normalisation rules each exist in exactly one place. A reader who disagrees with either can change it and see every conclusion in sections 4 and 7 move accordingly.
– Extending to forward multiples. Add a Fact_Estimates table at the same grain as Fact_Financials, carrying consensus forward EBITDA. No structural change is required to the model or the measures.
9.5  Reproducing this analysis in Power BI
The model imports into Power BI Desktop without a single Power Query edit, because every table in the source workbook is a named Excel table rather than a sheet range. The build sequence is:
– Get Data → Excel workbook. In the Navigator select the six named tables, not the sheets. Load.
– In Model view, create one-to-many single-direction relationships from Dim_Company[CompanyKey] to each fact table, and from Dim_FiscalYear[FYKey] to Fact_Financials and Fact_Operations. Leave Fact_Market and Fact_ESG unconnected to the year dimension.
– Select Dim_FiscalYear[FY Label] → Column tools → Sort by column → Sort Order. Without this, FY2023-24 sorts after FY2024-25.
– Create the measures at Appendix C. Tabular Editor 2 will bulk-create them from the listing; otherwise add them individually in the Modeling tab.
– Format: growth and margin measures 0.0%; multiples 0.0"x"; rupee measures #,0. Apply the theme at Appendix D.
– Set Edit interactions to Highlight on every visual, so selecting a company on one cross-filters the rest.
