Appendix C   Measure library
 
The measures below reproduce every figure in this report. They are written for Power BI's DAX engine and assume the model described at section 9.1. Every ratio uses DIVIDE rather than the division operator, which returns a blank on a zero denominator instead of an error.

Base aggregations
Revenue / EBITDA / PAT / Gross Debt / Cash / Net Debt / Total Equity / Capex / Finance Cost
Revenue      = SUM ( Fact_Financials[Revenue] )
EBITDA       = SUM ( Fact_Financials[EBITDA] )
PAT          = SUM ( Fact_Financials[PAT] )
Gross Debt   = SUM ( Fact_Financials[Gross Debt] )
Cash         = SUM ( Fact_Financials[Cash & Equiv] )
Net Debt     = SUM ( Fact_Financials[Net Debt] )
Total Equity = SUM ( Fact_Financials[Total Equity] )
Capex        = SUM ( Fact_Financials[Capex] )
Finance Cost = SUM ( Fact_Financials[Finance Cost] )
 
Market Cap
Market Cap =
CALCULATE (
   SUMX ( Fact_Market, Fact_Market[Close Price] * Fact_Market[Shares Outstanding] ),
   REMOVEFILTERS ( Dim_FiscalYear )
)
Market capitalisation is a point-in-time observation. Without REMOVEFILTERS it blanks whenever a prior fiscal year is selected.
Period selection
Selected FY / Selected FY Sort
Selected FY =
VAR _Sel = SELECTEDVALUE ( Dim_FiscalYear[FYKey] )
VAR _Latest =
   CALCULATE ( MAX ( Dim_FiscalYear[FYKey] ),
       FILTER ( ALL ( Dim_FiscalYear ), Dim_FiscalYear[Is Latest FY] = "Yes" ) )
RETURN COALESCE ( _Sel, _Latest )
 
Selected FY Sort =
CALCULATE ( MAX ( Dim_FiscalYear[Sort Order] ),
   FILTER ( ALL ( Dim_FiscalYear ), Dim_FiscalYear[FYKey] = [Selected FY] ) )
 
Prior-year retrievers
Revenue PY =
CALCULATE ( [Revenue],
   FILTER ( ALL ( Dim_FiscalYear ),
       Dim_FiscalYear[Sort Order] = [Selected FY Sort] - 1 ) )
 
-- EBITDA PY, PAT PY and Net Debt PY follow the identical pattern.
Dim_FiscalYear is a text key rather than a date table, so DATEADD and SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR are unavailable. The measures step on Sort Order instead.
Growth
Growth and CAGR
Revenue Growth YoY % = DIVIDE ( [Revenue] - [Revenue PY], ABS ( [Revenue PY] ) )
EBITDA Growth YoY %  = DIVIDE ( [EBITDA]  - [EBITDA PY],  ABS ( [EBITDA PY] ) )
PAT Growth YoY %     = DIVIDE ( [PAT]     - [PAT PY],     ABS ( [PAT PY] ) )
 
Revenue CAGR 2Y % =
VAR _End = [Revenue]
VAR _Start =
   CALCULATE ( [Revenue],
       FILTER ( ALL ( Dim_FiscalYear ),
           Dim_FiscalYear[Sort Order] = [Selected FY Sort] - 2 ) )
RETURN IF ( _Start > 0 && _End > 0, ( _End / _Start ) ^ ( 1 / 2 ) - 1 )
ABS on the denominator prevents a sign flip producing a growth rate with the wrong direction where a prior-period value is negative.
Profitability
Margin, returns and cover
EBITDA Margin %   = DIVIDE ( [EBITDA], [Revenue] )
PAT Margin %      = DIVIDE ( [PAT], [Revenue] )
ROE %             = DIVIDE ( [PAT], [Total Equity] )
ROCE %            = DIVIDE ( [EBITDA], [Total Equity] + [Gross Debt] )
Interest Cover    = DIVIDE ( [EBITDA], [Finance Cost] )
Self-Funding Gap  = [EBITDA] - [Capex]
 
Leverage
Ratios and bands
Net Debt to EBITDA   = DIVIDE ( [Net Debt], [EBITDA] )
Net Debt to Equity   = DIVIDE ( [Net Debt], [Total Equity] )
Gross Debt to Equity = DIVIDE ( [Gross Debt], [Total Equity] )
Net Gearing %        = DIVIDE ( [Net Debt], [Net Debt] + [Total Equity] )
Is Net Cash          = IF ( [Net Debt] < 0, "Net cash", "Net debt" )
 
Leverage Band =
VAR _x = [Net Debt to EBITDA]
RETURN SWITCH ( TRUE (),
   ISBLANK ( _x ), "No data",
   _x < 0, "Net cash",
   _x < 3, "Comfortable",
   _x < 6, "Watch",
   "Stretched" )
 
Leverage Band Colour =
SWITCH ( [Leverage Band],
   "Net cash", "#2E7D5B", "Comfortable", "#7FD1A8",
   "Watch", "#C0801A", "Stretched", "#B03A3A", "#6B7B85" )
The 3.0x and 6.0x thresholds exist only here. Changing them updates every band, colour and conclusion in section 4.
Valuation
Latest-year anchors
Net Debt Latest FY =
CALCULATE ( [Net Debt],
   FILTER ( ALL ( Dim_FiscalYear ), Dim_FiscalYear[Is Latest FY] = "Yes" ) )
 
-- EBITDA Latest FY, Revenue Latest FY, PAT Latest FY and Equity Latest FY
-- follow the identical pattern.
Pairing a live market capitalisation with a stale year's net debt would be wrong, so net debt is pinned to the latest reported year.
Multiples
Enterprise Value = [Market Cap] + [Net Debt Latest FY]
EV to EBITDA     = DIVIDE ( [Enterprise Value], [EBITDA Latest FY] )
EV to Revenue    = DIVIDE ( [Enterprise Value], [Revenue Latest FY] )
PE Ratio         = DIVIDE ( [Market Cap], [PAT Latest FY] )
PB Ratio         = DIVIDE ( [Market Cap], [Equity Latest FY] )
 
Operational Capacity MW =
CALCULATE ( SUM ( Fact_Operations[Operational RE Capacity MW] ),
   FILTER ( ALL ( Dim_FiscalYear ), Dim_FiscalYear[Is Latest FY] = "Yes" ) )
 
EV per MW (Rs cr) = DIVIDE ( [Enterprise Value], [Operational Capacity MW] )
 
Peer Median EV to EBITDA = MEDIANX ( ALL ( Dim_Company ), [EV to EBITDA] )
 
EV to EBITDA vs Peer Median % =
DIVIDE ( [EV to EBITDA] - [Peer Median EV to EBITDA], [Peer Median EV to EBITDA] )
 
ESG
Composite, coverage and correlation
ESG Composite =
CALCULATE ( AVERAGE ( Fact_ESG[ESG Composite] ), REMOVEFILTERS ( Dim_FiscalYear ) )
 
ESG Agencies Covering =
CALCULATE ( SUM ( Fact_ESG[Agencies Covering] ), REMOVEFILTERS ( Dim_FiscalYear ) )
 
ESG Coverage Warning =
VAR _n = [ESG Agencies Covering]
RETURN SWITCH ( TRUE (),
   ISBLANK ( _n ) || _n = 0, "No third-party rating located",
   _n = 1, "Single-agency score - low confidence",
   _n = 2, "Two agencies - moderate confidence",
   "Multi-agency - reasonable confidence" )
 
ESG vs Valuation Correlation =
VAR _t =
   FILTER (
       ADDCOLUMNS ( ALL ( Dim_Company[Company] ),
           "@esg", [ESG Composite], "@ev", [EV to EBITDA] ),
       NOT ISBLANK ( [@esg] ) && NOT ISBLANK ( [@ev] ) )
VAR _n = COUNTROWS ( _t )
VAR _mx = AVERAGEX ( _t, [@esg] )
VAR _my = AVERAGEX ( _t, [@ev] )
VAR _cov = SUMX ( _t, ( [@esg] - _mx ) * ( [@ev] - _my ) )
VAR _sx = SQRT ( SUMX ( _t, ( [@esg] - _mx ) ^ 2 ) )
VAR _sy = SQRT ( SUMX ( _t, ( [@ev] - _my ) ^ 2 ) )
RETURN IF ( _n >= 3 && _sx > 0 && _sy > 0, DIVIDE ( _cov, _sx * _sy ) )
The correlation measure requires at least three rated observations before it returns a value, which is why NTPC Green's absence is visible rather than silently averaged away.
