Appendix F   Limitations
 
Set out plainly, because a screening document that hides its weak points is worse than one that has none.

1 · The set is not comparable, and no adjustment fixes that
Four business models on one value chain. EV/Revenue carries no cross-sectional meaning here, and EBITDA margin measures the model rather than the performance. The report flags this wherever it applies, but a reader extracting a single table without the surrounding text will draw wrong conclusions.
2 · Estimated balance-sheet splits
Gross debt and total equity for Tata Power, NTPC Green and Suzlon are reconciled estimates derived from reported leverage ratios. They were validated against independently published price-to-book and price-to-earnings ratios to within 3% (section 9.3), and Tata Power's derived net debt to equity resolves to exactly the reported 1.18x. They should nonetheless be replaced with annual-report figures once all FY2025-26 reports are filed.
3 · Adani Green's FY2024-25 profit after tax
Taken as the sum of four reported quarterly consolidated net profits (₹1,848 crore). The annual reported figure may differ on non-controlling-interest treatment. This makes the FY2025-26 PAT decline of 15% the least reliable figure on the growth page, and it should be verified against the annual report before being relied upon. The direction of travel is corroborated independently by the December 2025 quarterly loss and by the scale of the capital expenditure.
4 · FY2023-24 is the weakest year in the model
It exists to enable a two-year compound growth rate. Individual FY2023-24 line items should not be quoted standalone.
5 · Mixed valuation dates
Suzlon's price is the 22 July 2026 close; the other three are 24 July 2026. No 24 July quote was retrievable for Suzlon. The effect is immaterial at these ranges but is recorded for completeness. Suzlon subsequently traded materially lower on 28 July 2026, its Q1 FY2026-27 results date.
6 · ESG composites rest on thin coverage
One to three agencies per company, with agency methodologies known to correlate weakly with one another. The composite is a screening flag, not a valuation input. One company has no rating at all and is excluded from the correlation rather than imputed.
7 · No forward estimates and no contingency provision
The report contains no consensus forecasts, no discounted cash flow and no target prices. Tata Power's outstanding SIAC arbitration award of USD 490.32 million is disclosed but not provided for in any multiple. Suzlon's SEBI penalty is likewise disclosed but not modelled.
8 · What would strengthen the next iteration
– Quarterly grain. Replacing Dim_FiscalYear with a period dimension supports quarterly trending without structural change.
– A Fact_Estimates table carrying consensus forward EBITDA, enabling forward multiples alongside trailing.
– Segment-level revenue for Tata Power, the only name where a consolidated figure conceals the story.
– Cost of debt by company, which would convert section 4 from a stock measure into a coverage measure.
– Order-book conversion tracking for Suzlon, the single largest driver of its forward numbers.
 